From 2a6fb39cb9c62d90d9c538a2471dfff1e8b6db71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:16:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): close fairness capture review lifecycle gaps
 [daveey]

Resolve the five findings left open in #3687. Scoped serving and dispatcher
startup acquire close ownership only for newly created epochs. Await boot
and close through cancellation so late thread results are cleaned up and
the singleton lease releases even when close fails. Validate Unix runtime
prerequisites before capture IO; disabled capture remains inert. Restore or
remove the plan when connection or journal admission refuses, while keeping
budget-first admission and retaining the plan after successful arming.

Root cause: shared epoch lookup was mistaken for lifetime ownership;
async cancellation was mistaken for worker termination; optional runtime
IO assumed Unix; plan publication preceded journal admission without undo.

Proof: focused ownership/platform/cancellation/arm tests fail on original
53480c6dc085b55617a75ea6ac975ceda015e38f source and pass with fixes.
Writer final producer and reader custody, armed export refusal, and budget
mismatch tests each kill their targeted mutants. Full consumer selection:
78 files / 1155 tests pass; scripts/check all 21 checks pass. Also cover real
gateway slash dispatch, reversed serving/tenure ownership, connection
refusal and drain failure after arm. No live activation or default change.

